-- title:
--   Unramifiedness of X₀(M')→ X(1) away from j=0,1728
-- statement:
--   Let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K_0$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the quotients $f/g$ of the Laurent series attached to integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_0(M')$ (with denominator series non-zero). Let $j_0 \in K_0$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is the image under the same coefficientwise map of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the series $q^{-1}$ times the rational numerator power series of the $j$-invariant. Let $w$ be a place of $K_0$ over $L$, i.e. a proper valuation subring of $K_0$ containing the image of $L$ and whose ring is a principal ideal ring, and suppose that the associated order function satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_w(j_0) = 0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_w(j_0 - 1728) = 0$. Then the ramification index of $w$ along the inclusion of $L(j_0) = L(\{j_0\})$ into $K_0$ — the infimum of the positive integers of the form $\operatorname{ord}_w(f)$ for non-zero $f \in L(j_0)$ — equals $1$.
--
--   This is the assertion that the covering $X_0(M') \to X(1)$ is unramified, in characteristic zero, at every place of the function field whose $j$-value is neither $0$ nor $1728$ nor $\infty$, the classical reason being the triviality of the stabiliser in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of a non-elliptic point of the upper half-plane. It feeds the unramifiedness statement for the polynomial chart of $X_0$ at places of height one at which the $j$-coordinate avoids the exceptional values.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ramificationIndexAlong_val_adjoin_eq_one_of_ord_eq_zero_of_ord_sub_eq_zero_laurentBaseChange_gamma0.lean

